! conclusion: This is a problem-stating node: agents can find material humans have not seen while lacking a mechanism to teach it back.
  + context: Minted as a marked self-derived fallback after A5's external-first search found related peer-learning claims but no statement of this specific problem.
  + IF:
    Agents search and experiment faster than their human collaborators.
  + HOWEVER:
    The problem, verbatim from the source pattern: “The bottleneck inverts: the agent finds things the human hasn't seen, but has no mechanism to teach them back.” (source: futon3 library/gauntlet/teaching-inversion.flexiarg:19)
  + THEN:
    Treat this node as the landing point for agent-to-human teaching mechanisms.
  + BECAUSE:
    The source class makes the circular provenance mechanically visible.
